    {
      "@id": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:70e32e7388b156b6504e815be398953d6521a74536b8c3f4c1c87d64f0bdf5d1",
      "@type": "rkaf:Artifact",
      "rkaf:hasArtifactIdentifier": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:70e32e7388b156b6504e815be398953d6521a74536b8c3f4c1c87d64f0bdf5d1",
      "rkaf:artifactIdentifierScheme": "rkaf:urn-persistent",
      "rkaf:hasContentDigest": "sha256:be033b4a92ee96b5c071301fcef4ac28751256689e4101c3f3bcf1a7962d7d12",
      "dcterms:format": "application/json",
      "dcterms:description": "{\"action\":\"\",\"actor\":\"\",\"alternative_quotes\":[],\"applies_to\":[],\"assertion_ids\":[\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:eb5fba8ffd9492bbcb762c79bfdd069398aafcd1f73ff6be54fbb8f3991c5163\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:65f949ae668ec05d7f6759e8183158fc767fef7028ee4588fea007db291a711a\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:1b84a99b8c2af74abb31f3bd27d5016266040385a6a0a57125a4b07cc530ed35\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:f3ead21e9a3aa59bb73bbe5e163c8341fd295a22cb0d8f72c8fbf02dfb31810e\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:c34d2249fa7ac9087187db2f7c657f2df497c92106dc444fa06d085acf65cbfb\"],\"choice_quote\":\"\",\"choice_text\":\"\",\"claimants\":[],\"concepts\":[],\"context_quotes\":[\"(a) An eligible employee is an employee of a covered employer who:\\n\\n(1) Has been employed by the employer for at least 12 months, and\\n\\n(2) Has been employed for at least 1,250 hours of service during the 12-month period immediately preceding the commencement of the leave ( see § 825.801 for special hours of service requirements for airline flight crew employees), and\\n\\n(3) Is employed at a worksite where 50 or more employees are employed by the employer within 75 miles of that worksite. See § 825.105(b) regarding employees who work outside the U.S.\"],\"effective_periods\":[],\"end\":5933,\"evidence\":[{\"end\":5933,\"field\":\"summary\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:5370:5933:sha256-47eba493b53486ba093d7a6299a7e50e0816dd5ddeb5de830bd5be07e6f5395c\",\"quote\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"start\":5370},{\"end\":5933,\"field\":\"logic_text\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:5370:5933:sha256-47eba493b53486ba093d7a6299a7e50e0816dd5ddeb5de830bd5be07e6f5395c\",\"quote\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"start\":5370},{\"end\":5538,\"field\":\"modality\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:5526:5538:sha256-55bfba7dfd23c6b431a8dcaed943bb701e1b6c00cd6580bdd732544bf80f57e9\",\"quote\":\"must be made\",\"start\":5526},{\"end\":5933,\"field\":\"scope_text:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:5370:5933:sha256-47eba493b53486ba093d7a6299a7e50e0816dd5ddeb5de830bd5be07e6f5395c\",\"quote\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"start\":5370},{\"end\":590,\"field\":\"context:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:37:590:sha256-e43d03081e43a5cd56466e06b1489af91ab5a4d901b3a2068f64e68e4fa8e5dd\",\"quote\":\"(a) An eligible employee is an employee of a covered employer who:\\n\\n(1) Has been employed by the employer for at least 12 months, and\\n\\n(2) Has been employed for at least 1,250 hours of service during the 12-month period immediately preceding the commencement of the leave ( see § 825.801 for special hours of service requirements for airline flight crew employees), and\\n\\n(3) Is employed at a worksite where 50 or more employees are employed by the employer within 75 miles of that worksite. See § 825.105(b) regarding employees who work outside the U.S.\",\"start\":37}],\"id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:70e32e7388b156b6504e815be398953d6521a74536b8c3f4c1c87d64f0bdf5d1\",\"jurisdiction\":\"\",\"jurisdiction_quote\":\"\",\"kind\":\"requirement\",\"logic_text\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"meaning_assertion_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:c34d2249fa7ac9087187db2f7c657f2df497c92106dc444fa06d085acf65cbfb\",\"modality\":\"must\",\"modality_quote\":\"must be made\",\"object\":\"\",\"occurrence_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:occurrence:cda91db471a0e14a52af5a7a4d3b43b0950fb5a8b44692c3bf3d54a892484dff\",\"origin\":\"aiSuggested\",\"quote\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"references\":[\"§ 825.300(b)\"],\"relation\":\"none\",\"rule_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:rule:8dda62a56e1f5277004a6b8c0a9d28bb42b709a374ab4263253d4849d497955f\",\"scope_quotes\":[\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\"],\"scope_text\":\"For determining whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and total of at least 12 months of employment\",\"section_id\":\"section-1\",\"start\":5370,\"summary\":\"The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start, and if an employee is on non-FMLA leave when meeting 12-month eligibility, any portion taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after meeting it becomes FMLA leave (referencing § 825.300(b) for eligibility notice rules).\",\"target_ids\":[],\"typed_values\":[]}",
